---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { ogPathFor } from '../data/og'
import { principles, proposedPrinciple, smells, factoryUrl, deskSetupUrl, ouroMdInstall } from '../data/principles.mjs'
import { labelFor } from '../data/readiness.mjs'

const title = 'How do you effectively collaborate with agents? | Ouroboros'
const description = "Here's how I believe it works, what I use to support it, and what you can try."

const deskLabel = labelFor('desk-claude-code-macos')
const ouroMdLabel = labelFor('ouro-md')

const link = 'text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 hover:text-glow transition-colors'
const card = 'rounded-2xl border border-canopy/40 bg-deep/70 p-6'
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogPathFor('/')} canonical="https://ouroboros.bot/">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "How do you effectively collaborate with agents?",
      "url": "https://ouroboros.bot/",
      "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Ari Mendelow" },
      "dateModified": "2026-10-10"
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero: the question, the short answer, and the three smells as the way in -->
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 pt-28 pb-14 md:pt-40 md:pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.25fr_1fr] lg:items-center">
      <div>
        <h1 class="heading-lead animate-fade-up">How do you effectively collaborate with agents?</h1>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-mist leading-relaxed mt-6 max-w-[46ch] animate-fade-up stagger-1">
          Here's how I believe it works, what I use to support it, and what you can try. The short version: talk through what you want together, hand over whole outcomes, write down what matters, give the agent real authority with clear limits, and check the actual result.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-8 animate-fade-up stagger-2">
          <a href="/approach/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-bone text-void px-5 py-3 font-medium hover:bg-scale transition-colors">Read the approach &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/brief/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-canopy text-bone px-5 py-3 font-medium hover:border-scale hover:text-scale transition-colors">Hand this to your agent</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class={`${card} grid gap-4 animate-fade-up stagger-3`} aria-labelledby="smells-heading">
        <h2 id="smells-heading" class="caption-mono">Three smells that something's off</h2>
        {smells.map((smell) => (
          <div class="grid gap-1 pb-4 border-b border-dashed border-canopy/50">
            <p class="font-display text-2xl text-bone leading-tight">{smell.name}</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-mist">{smell.short}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
        <p class="text-sm text-mist">Each one means the agent is borrowing your hands, your memory or your nerve.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The three acts: the spine -->
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-14 md:py-20 border-t border-canopy/15" aria-labelledby="acts-heading">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-8">
      <div class="grid gap-3 max-w-3xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Where we are</span>
        <h2 id="acts-heading" class="heading-sub">We are between Acts 2 and 3. Keeping agents oriented is still settling, and the push now is on designing and measuring the work itself.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-canopy/40 bg-void/60 p-6 grid gap-3 content-start">
          <span class="caption-mono">Act 1 · Capability</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone leading-tight">Can an agent do real work on a computer?</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">Yes, well enough. What's left over is a habit: we still do by hand what the agent could have done.</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-1">Essay: <a href="/essays/stop-being-the-glue/" class={link}>Stop being the glue</a></p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-scale/70 bg-deep p-6 grid gap-3 content-start">
          <span class="caption-mono !text-scale">Act 2 · Orientation · settling</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone leading-tight">Can it stay coherent across time, people and sessions?</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">Still settling, for people and agents alike. The five principles below are the human side, Desk and Ouro MD are the system side, and the harness is where we experiment with what agents need.</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-1 flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
            <a href="/approach/" class={link}>The approach</a>
            <a href="/desk/" class={link}>Desk</a>
            <a href="/ouro-md/" class={link}>Ouro MD</a>
            <a href="/lab/" class={link}>Lab</a>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-scale/70 bg-deep p-6 grid gap-3 content-start">
          <span class="caption-mono !text-scale">Act 3 · Designed work · where the push is</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone leading-tight">Can we design and measure the work itself?</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">The industry is pushing here, and so are we. Others use "software factory" as a name. Ours brings the Lean methodology with it: waste named from evidence, an alarm built to stop the line on a defect, and fixes checked against later data once there's enough of it. It's built to work with any factory setup, not only ours. Designed for many, proven on one so far. It's early, and it's public.</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-1"><a href={factoryUrl} class={link}>The factory &rarr;</a></p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Act 2, the human side: Ari's five principles, plus the proposed sixth -->
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-14 md:py-20 border-t border-canopy/15" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-8">
      <div class="grid gap-3">
        <span class="eyebrow">Act 2, the human side</span>
        <h2 id="principles-heading" class="heading-sub">Five principles</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-px rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-canopy/40 bg-canopy/40 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {principles.map((p) => (
          <a href={`/approach/#${p.id}`} class="group bg-deep p-6 grid gap-2 content-start hover:bg-undergrowth transition-colors">
            <span class="font-mono text-sm text-scale">{p.n}</span>
            <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone leading-tight group-hover:text-scale transition-colors">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-mist">{p.summary}</p>
            <span class="text-sm text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 mt-1">Read more &rarr;</span>
          </a>
        ))}
        <a href={`/approach/#${proposedPrinciple.id}`} class="group p-6 grid gap-2 content-start bg-[color-mix(in_srgb,var(--color-deep)_88%,var(--color-amber))] hover:bg-undergrowth transition-colors">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-amber">{proposedPrinciple.n}</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone leading-tight group-hover:text-scale transition-colors">{proposedPrinciple.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">{proposedPrinciple.summary}</p>
          <span class="text-sm text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 mt-1">Read more &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What supports this -->
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-14 md:py-20 border-t border-canopy/15" aria-labelledby="supports-heading">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-8">
      <div class="grid gap-3">
        <span class="eyebrow">Act 2, the system side</span>
        <h2 id="supports-heading" class="heading-sub">What supports this</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <a href="/desk/" class={`${card} group grid gap-3 content-start hover:border-scale transition-colors`}>
          <img src="/brand/desk-icon.svg" width="48" height="48" alt="" class="mark-tile w-12 h-12" />
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone group-hover:text-scale transition-colors">Desk</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">Keeps these principles in the setup instead of in your head.</p>
          <span class="text-sm text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40">About Desk &rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/ouro-md/" class={`${card} group grid gap-3 content-start hover:border-scale transition-colors`}>
          <img src="/brand/ouro-md-icon.png" width="48" height="48" alt="" class="mark-tile w-12 h-12" />
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone group-hover:text-scale transition-colors">Ouro MD</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">Where I read and answer what my agents write.</p>
          <span class="text-sm text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40">About Ouro MD &rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a href={factoryUrl} class={`${card} group grid gap-3 content-start hover:border-scale transition-colors`}>
          <span class="mark-mask w-12 h-12 text-scale" style="--mark:url(/brand/ouro-silhouette.svg)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone group-hover:text-scale transition-colors">The factory</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">Our public record of how the work actually goes, misses included.</p>
          <span class="text-sm text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40">Open the factory &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Try it today -->
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-14 md:py-20 border-t border-canopy/15" aria-labelledby="try-heading">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-8">
      <div class="grid gap-3">
        <span class="eyebrow">What you can do next</span>
        <h2 id="try-heading" class="heading-sub">Try it today</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class={`${card} grid gap-3 content-start`}>
          <span class="tag tag-plain justify-self-start">No install</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone">Hand this to your agent</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">A one-page brief with the five principles, written for your agent to read. Paste it into whatever agent you use now.</p>
          <a href="/brief/" class={`${link} text-sm`}>Get the brief &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class={`${card} grid gap-3 content-start`}>
          <span class={`tag ${deskLabel.tone} justify-self-start`}>{deskLabel.label}</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone">Desk</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">Give your agent one link and say "set this up". Claude Code on macOS is the tested path.</p>
          <p class="agent-text !text-xs">{deskSetupUrl}</p>
          <a href="/desk/" class={`${link} text-sm`}>What it does and where it runs &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class={`${card} grid gap-3 content-start`}>
          <span class={`tag ${ouroMdLabel.tone} justify-self-start`}>{ouroMdLabel.label}</span>
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl text-bone">Ouro MD</h3>
          <p class="text-mist">Live file updates, with quiet marks where your agent changed things.</p>
          <p class="agent-text !text-xs">{ouroMdInstall}</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-mist">macOS 13 or later.</p>
          <a href="/ouro-md/" class={`${link} text-sm`}>About Ouro MD &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
